<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Castro de El Raso</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Castro de El Raso is an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/iron-age">Iron Age</a> hillfort at Candeleda in the province of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/avila">Ávila</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, on the southern slopes of the Sierra de Gredos. Occupied by the Vettones from about the 4th century BCE until it was abandoned around the time of the Roman conquest in the 1st century BCE, it has yielded walls, gateways and stone houses, some reconstructed for visitors.</p></div>
